<title>LEBANON: Lebanon 1996 trade deficit widens by $53.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Lebanon 1996 trade deficit widens by $53.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's 1996 trade deficit widened by $53.3 million to $6,532.3 million from $6,479 million according to customs figures released on Thursday.</p>
<p>According to the figures, December's trade deficit reached $654 million, up from $562 million in November.</p>
<p>Customs revenues rose to 1,632 billion Lebanese pounds in 1996 compared with 1,321 billion pounds a year earlier.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE	Dec 96     Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p>Monthly</p>
<p>    Exports		     83.0	100.0	   87.0</p>
<p>    Imports		    737.0	662.0	  646.0</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -654.0     -562.0	 -559.0</p>
<p>Year-to-date</p>
<p>    Exports		  1,017.0	 935.3	 824.0</p>
<p>    Imports		  7,549.0     6,821.6     7,303.0</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -6,532.3    -5,886.3    -6,479.0</p>
<p>Note - Figures in millions of U.S. dollars.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,549.25 Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
